Hardware-cursor NDRV for the ATI Radeon 9700 (ati-radeon-9700 / ppc_mac_gpu)
============================================================================

pc-bios/qemu_vga_hwc.ndrv is QemuMacDrivers' qemu_vga.ndrv (qemu_vga.orig.ndrv
here) with its hardware-cursor stubs patched to drive the device's cursor
registers at MMIO BAR + 0xFF00. See the docstring in build.py and the register
list in hw/display/ppc_mac_gpu.c.

Origin: firmware/src/ndrv of https://github.com/linuxkid473/ppc-osx-vgpu
(GPL-2.0). Local change: the SetHardwareCursor routine also sends the cursor
hotspot (IOHardwareCursorInfo.cursorHotSpotX/Y) through register 0x1C, so the
host can put the pointer on the cursor's tip instead of the image's corner.

Rebuild (plain Python 3, no other dependencies):

    python3 build.py qemu_vga.orig.ndrv ../../pc-bios/qemu_vga_hwc.ndrv
